# of the form type=value. Types use common short names like C, ST, L, O, OU,
# CN, emailAddress, serialNumber, street, postalCode, givenName, surname, title,
# GN, SN, DC, UID, etc. Values should avoid commas and equals (unless escaped).
# We keep values ASCII printable and avoid problematic characters.
#
# We aim to produce a variety of valid DNs with:
# - single- and multi-RDN entries
# - multi-valued RDNs joined by '+' (e.g., CN=example+UID=1001)
# - different attribute types and lengths
# - inclusion of digits and safe punctuation in values
# - varied country codes (2 letters) and optional attributes
#
# Output is a bytes object containing a NUL-terminated C string or not?
# The stubs pass std::string.c_str() and in two places they manually append a NUL.
# mbedtls_x509_string_to_names expects a null-terminated C string.
# FUZZ framework likely treats provided buffer as-is; we'll include a terminating NUL
